From 29830219811f9eac7ab4c311e350b91dc6714fcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:19:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] Send photos and videos in the chat and play the
 received videos

A clip button next to the text field takes a photo or records a video
with the camera (at most two minutes) or picks one from the library. Files
above 50 MB, the server's limit for videos, are not sent; a refusal by the
server (format, size, virus scan) shows its reason. Received videos are
downloaded with the login to a temporary file, played full screen and the
file is deleted when the player closes, so health videos do not stay on
the phone.

Correction to "Chat with the professionals from the app": the explicit
UTF-8 decoding of the answer is not needed. The server sends
application/json, which the http package already reads as UTF-8; only the
test answers without a content type came out as Latin-1. The tests now
send the content type the server sends.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VRSTuUkoebWWM2DLbPZAvR
